# left unattended: nothing it meets is an exception.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE FOUR PHASES, each answering to a checked theorem
#
#   1. SYNC       publish and absorb.  Owner rule 2026-08-14.
#   2. GATE       check every module SEPARATELY and record its own exit
#                 code.  Never the aggregate alone.
#   3. LEDGER     append the cycle: greens, fibers, and the walk frontier.
#   4. DRAW       cut a fresh uncurated door so whatever attaches next
#                 does not enter through the conspicuous documents.
#
# Phase 2 is per-module because this repository has produced the same
# defect twice in one day in opposite directions:  a WARNING read as an
# error (`UnsupportedIndexedMatch`, correction 0395), and a MISSING NAME
# read as a green for a day (`injectSuc`, msg 0456), plus a BUILD.md
# claiming "every module, exit 0" while checking a minority of them.
# All three survive any check that looks at aggregate output instead of
# `$?` per module.
#
#     A green is an exit code, and only for what was actually run.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEDGER ROW SEMANTICS — exact, 2026-08-16 (state-vs-event discipline)
#
# One row = one EVENT: "this container, carrying this toolchain, invoked
# these checks at this time and observed these exit codes."  A row is
# never a STATE of the mathematics.  Reading it as one is the same error
# corrected at the top of this header — a claim about a state, evidenced
# by an event — and it happened in this very ledger: the
# 2026-08-14T17:19Z row read "315 modules, 0 green, 315 fibers" as if
# the corpus had died in twelve hours.  What actually happened is two
# superimposed events that the old schema could not distinguish:
#   (a) the tree genuinely grew 87 -> 315 modules that day (sibling
#       swarm landings; verified from git, not from this ledger), and
#   (b) the cycle ran in a fresh container with NO `agda` ON PATH, so
#       every per-module invocation exited 127 (command not found) —
#       the aggregate's 127 is the tell; Agda itself, when present,
#       exits 0 or 1, never 127.
# Zero mathematics was checked and zero mathematics was broken.  The
# row recorded the container and called it the corpus.
#
# Columns (tab-separated, header row first, append-only after that):
#   utc            when the row was appended (event time, UTC).
#   cycle          ordinal = number of data rows before this one.  A
#                  count of ledger events, not a clock: a gap in `utc`
#                  is silence (no machine ran), never "missed cycles".
#   toolchain      the checker that produced this row's exit codes,
#                  e.g. `agda-2.6.3`, or `absent` when no agda was on
#                  PATH.  The tree's pin is Agda 2.8.0 + cubical v0.9
#                  (formal/cubical/BUILD.md "Toolchain"); a row whose
#                  toolchain differs from the pin carries version-skew
#                  fibers that are evidence about the SKEW, not the
#                  tree, and BUILD.md "Where the skew bites" must be
#                  read next to it.
#   modules        how many modules were actually invoked this cycle.
#                  0 when toolchain=absent: a check that cannot start
#                  is 0 checks performed, not N failed ones.
#   green          count of exit 0.  An exit code, only for what was
#                  actually run — never parsed output, never inferred.
#
#   [CORRECTION 2026-08-23 — THE EXIT-CODE RULE BELOW IS NOT EXACT, and the
